// =====================================================================
// /app/briefs/brief-builder — Brief Builder · Vibe Code block.
//
// v3 — the Brief & Content design over the proven details engine.
// One white document (the page) holds the brief name and every Bible
// section; the right rail holds Details (the old Overview), Sections
// and Modules. Section names, fields and modules come straight from
// the Notion Brief Bible (Briefs Sections + Field Reference + Modules
// databases) — 19 sections, 20 modules.
//
// Layout:
//   Top bar     — Brief · Submissions · Invites switch the page;
//                 Preview · Share · Publish on the right
//   The page    — editable title + the brief's sections in order.
//                 Every section is added from the rail, movable
//                 up/down, collapsible, and multi-field sections
//                 carry a parts menu (page + rail) so the user
//                 decides which fields show.
//   The rail    — Details (status, review mode, visibility,
//                 thumbnail, creator info) · Sections (the Bible,
//                 short line + tooltip) · Modules (blueprint pulls
//                 + generic inserts that append into Extra).
//
// Storage: per-field saves on blur; section_order (cp3Rg) persists
// the section order AND the visible parts per section, encoded as
// "key:part+part,key2". description (FCBU5) is rewritten on every
// save with the whole brief compiled to PLAIN TEXT for the Vertex
// review engine. Old briefs whose description holds the legacy JSON
// get migrated into the section fields on first open. awareness and
// channel have no UI here by design — their stored values feed the
// Write-with-AI context only.
//
// SOFTR CONFIG REQUIRED:
//   1. Page: the brief detail page (recordId in URL).
//   2. Source tab: briefs + accounts + submissions + members tables
//      AND the OpenRouter REST API datasource (Authorization:
//      Bearer <key> lives there). After connecting, ask the block AI
//      to replace REPLACE_SUBMISSIONS_DS_ID / REPLACE_MEMBERS_DS_ID
//      with the connected datasource ids.
//   3. Actions tab: re-sync Update Record after pasting — the write
//      list changed (make_sure joins it; offer fee/commission/gift
//      in; content type, channel, awareness out).
//   4. The /briefs/inspo-picker, /swipe-picker, /assign-brief and
//      /brief-invite modal pages, same as details.
// =====================================================================

