    worked: `<p><b>Watch these before you film:</b></p><ul><li><b>[Top-performing ad, link]:</b> the oil-lift demo in the first two seconds. The result is on screen before a word is said, that's what stops the scroll.</li><li><b>[Past submission that landed, link]:</b> the matte-at-3pm proof shot. The makeup-intact moment does the selling without a claim.</li><li><b>[Swipe file, link]:</b> the raw, phone-propped yap style. This is the energy and finish we're after, not polished.</li></ul>`,
    placeholder: `<p><b>Watch these before you film:</b></p><ul><li><b>[Reference clip, link]:</b> [what to notice, and why it works].</li><li><b>[Reference clip, link]:</b> [what to notice, and why it works].</li><li><b>[Reference clip, link]:</b> [what to notice, and why it works].</li></ul>`,
    prompt: "You are writing the Examples section for [BRAND NAME or WEBSITE URL], for a [CREATOR TYPE] creator. Hand over reference content that shows what good looks like. For each reference, give the clip (or a link placeholder), what to notice, and why it works. Close on how to use them: match the standard, borrow the structure, make it their own. Pull references that fit the chosen visual format. No em dashes, British spelling."
