  {
    n: 12, name: "Props", icon: "box", format: "bulletList",
    what: "The gather-before-you-film list: every item that needs to appear on camera, including anything the creator supplies themselves.",
    why: "A creator who realises the night before that they're missing a prop either delays or films without it. A clear list means every shot can be filmed.",
    includes: ["The product and its components (hero items)", "Supporting items the shots call for (water, mirror, tools, packaging)", "Creator-supplied items, with grouped examples to pick from"],
    worked: `<p><b>Items in the shots:</b></p><ul><li>Volcanic Roller</li><li>A small mirror</li><li>Tissue or loo roll (for the before, the blotting shot)</li><li>Your usual makeup, applied as normal</li><li>Good natural light, film near a window</li></ul>`,
    placeholder: `<p><b>Items in the shots:</b></p><ul><li>[Product and its components, the hero items]</li><li>[Supporting items the shots need, e.g. water, a mirror, packaging]</li><li>[Creator-supplied item], for example: [option], [option]</li></ul>`,
    prompt: "You are writing the Props section for [BRAND NAME or WEBSITE URL], for a [CREATOR TYPE] creator. Read the storyboard and list what has to be in frame: product and components (hero items), supporting items, and creator-supplied items with a few grouped examples so they pick something natural. A practical checklist, no padding. No em dashes, British spelling."
