  {
    n: 13, name: "Production Notes", icon: "video", format: "text",
    what: "The practical how-to-film, set by the chosen visual format: device, stabilisation, lighting, background, product handling, length, takes.",
    why: "The same script shot on a wobbly phone in bad light comes back unusable. These notes set the technical floor and carry the format's intent.",
    includes: ["Device and stabilisation", "Lighting: natural, window, or ring light", "Background: real and specific, or a clean set", "Product handling, length, takes"],
    worked: `<p><b>Production Notes (Problem / Solution Ad).</b> Shot on your phone on a tripod. Good lighting. Background should be real: your desk, your kitchen, your car. Hold the product casually at some point, like you grabbed it off the counter. Don't present it. Aim for a 30 to 60 second video in total, filmed in multiple takes.</p>`,
    placeholder: `<p><b>Production Notes ([Format]).</b> Shot on [device], [stabilisation]. [Lighting]. Background should be [real and specific, or clean set]. [How to handle the product]. Aim for a [length] video in total, filmed in [one take / multiple takes].</p>`,
    prompt: "You are writing the Production Notes section for [BRAND NAME or WEBSITE URL], for a [CREATOR TYPE] creator, in the [VISUAL FORMAT] format. Set every note by the format: device and stabilisation, lighting, background, product handling (casual, not presented), target length, takes. Polished format = tripod and clean light; raw format = handheld phone and window light on purpose. Short and practical. No em dashes, British spelling."
  },

  {
    n: 14, name: "Guidelines", icon: "shield-check", format: "bulletList",
    what: "The creator's dos and don'ts, generated from the format's thresholds and review agents. The creator sees three plain blocks; no numbers, no agent names.",
    why: "The \u201cmake sure you\u201d block tells creators exactly how to get approved, and because it's generated from the same settings Brieflee checks, the instructions and your quality bar are the same thing.",
